From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@cappuchino.xyz>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a523: attach display0 top to VO0

The TG5050 stock DT assigns vo0@5500000 to PCK-600 domain 3 (VO0).
The mainline display0 top node omitted this dependency. With no consumer,
genpd powers VO0 off during late init even though the TCON and DSI clocks
remain enabled and DRM still reports an active CRTC. Live register dumps
then read entirely as zero for both TCON-LCD1 and DSI1.

Describe the same power-domain dependency on tcon_top. Platform probing
will power the domain before the display-top driver touches registers and
keep it claimed while that device is bound. This addresses power-domain
ownership only; it does not claim to fix the remaining DE/DSI scanout bugs.

Source: TG5050 vendor kernel DT, /soc@3000000/vo0@5500000,
        power-domains = <&pck600 3>; mainline PD_VO0 is also 3.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a523.dtsi
@@ -825,6 +825,7 @@
 		tcon_top: tcon-top@5500000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h6-tcon-top";
 			reg = <0x05500000 0x1000>;
+			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_VO0>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_DISPLAY0_TOP>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_TCON_TV0>;
 			clock-names = "bus", "tcon-tv0";
